<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <section id="openfilter" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
            <label>OpenFilter</label>
            <tab>iranimij</tab>
            <resource>Iranimij_OpenFilter::config</resource>
            <group id="general" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>General</label>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enable OpenFilter</label>
                    <comment>Turns OpenFilter's layered navigation on for this scope. When off, Magento's own filters are shown.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="ajax" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Update results without reloading the page</label>
                    <comment>Filters, chips, sorting and paging swap the results in place. Every filter is still a normal link, so search engines and shoppers without JavaScript get the same pages.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="debug" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="90" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Debug mode</label>
                    <comment>Adds data-of-* attributes to the filter markup and writes the facet count strategy to var/log/openfilter.log. Keep it off in production.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="display" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="15" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Display</label>
                <field id="expanded_groups" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Filters open by default</label>
                    <comment>How many filters are expanded when the page loads. A filter set to "open" or "closed" in Catalog > OpenFilter > Filters keeps its own setting.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-zero-or-greater</validate>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\NonNegativeNumber</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="price_step" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Price slider step</label>
                    <comment>The slider moves in steps of this amount, in the currency the shopper sees.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-number validate-zero-or-greater</validate>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\NonNegativeNumber</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="layout" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Where filters show on desktop</label>
                    <comment>A bar above the products leaves the full width to the products; filters open as panels. Phones always use the filter drawer.</comment>
                    <source_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Source\Layout</source_model>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="apply_mode" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>When results update on desktop</label>
                    <comment>"After Show N products" lets shoppers pick several values first, then see the products in one step. Phones always work this way.</comment>
                    <source_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Source\ApplyMode</source_model>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="sticky" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Keep the sidebar in view while scrolling</label>
                    <comment>The filters stay next to the products while shoppers scroll a long list (sidebar layout only).</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="pagination" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="55" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>More products</label>
                    <comment>"Load more" adds the next page's products below the list; "As shoppers scroll" loads two pages on its own, then shows the button so the page footer stays reachable. The page links stay for search engines and without JavaScript.</comment>
                    <source_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Source\Pagination</source_model>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="quick_bar_size" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Quick filter bar above the products: values shown</label>
                    <comment>0 = no bar. One-click links to the values of the filters you mark with "In the quick filter bar" (filter form › How it behaves), picked values first, then the values with the most products.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-zero-or-greater</validate>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\NonNegativeNumber</backend_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="all_products" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="17" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>All Products page</label>
                <comment>Every product of the store view with the filters, on its own page (the store's root category; it must be an anchor category, as Magento's default root is).</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Show the All Products page</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="url_key" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>URL key</label>
                    <comment>Below the store's address, for example all-products or shop/all.html. A page that already has this address (a category, a CMS page) keeps it.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="title" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Page title and heading</label>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="seo" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="18" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>SEO</label>
                <field id="url_format" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Filter URLs on category pages</label>
                    <comment>Paths read like folders (women/tops/color-black,blue.html); query parameters are Magento's way (?color=black,blue). Old links of the other kind redirect (301). Search pages always use query parameters.</comment>
                    <source_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Source\UrlFormat</source_model>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="nofollow_threshold" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Ask search engines not to follow filter links from this many active values</label>
                    <comment>Keeps crawlers out of endless filter combinations. 0 = never.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-zero-or-greater</validate>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\NonNegativeNumber</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="max_active_values" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Most filter values active at once</label>
                    <comment>A URL with more values is redirected to the first ones and not indexed. Protects your crawl budget and page cache from bots. 0 = no limit.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-zero-or-greater</validate>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\NonNegativeNumber</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="meta_title" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Page title of filtered pages</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[For example <code>{filters} {category} | {store}</code>. {category} = category name, {filters} = the active values ("Red, Blue"), {store} = store name. Empty = Magento's title. Up to 60 characters show in search results.]]></comment>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="meta_description" translate="label comment" type="textarea" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Meta description of filtered pages</label>
                    <comment>Same placeholders. Empty = Magento's description. Up to 160 characters show in search results.</comment>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="h1" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Heading (H1) of filtered pages</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[For example <code>{filters} {category}</code>. Empty = the category name.]]></comment>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="sitemap" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="19" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>XML sitemap</label>
                <comment>Adds the filter pages search engines may index (one value of a filter marked "Let Google index pages filtered by this") to Magento's XML sitemap (Marketing > SEO &amp; Search > Site Map).</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Add indexable filter pages</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="min_products" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Only pages with at least this many products</label>
                    <comment>Thin pages with one or two products rarely rank and waste crawl budget.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\NonNegativeNumber</backend_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="max_urls" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Most filter pages per store view</label>
                    <comment>The pages with the most products come first. 0 = no limit.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-zero-or-greater</validate>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\NonNegativeNumber</backend_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="search" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Filter counts</label>
                <field id="count_strategy" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>How filter counts are computed</label>
                    <comment>Automatic picks the fastest method proven for your search engine. Both methods show the same numbers.</comment>
                    <source_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Source\CountStrategy</source_model>
                    <backend_model>Iranimij\OpenFilter\Model\Config\Backend\PageCacheValue</backend_model>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
